    slug: 'month-country-turgenev',
    intro: "A Month in the Country (1850, premiered 1872) is Ivan Turgenev's most celebrated play and one of the masterpieces of nineteenth-century Russian drama — the story of Natalya Petrovna, the wife of a provincial landowner, who falls in love with the young tutor of her son, and of the web of desire and jealousy that results. The play was too psychologically advanced for its time and was not performed until twenty-two years after it was written; it is now recognized as the direct precursor of Chekhov's dramatic method.",
