    intro: "Mumu (1852) is Ivan Turgenev's most famous short story and his most direct antiserfdom work — the story of Gerasim, a deaf-mute serf working as a porter in a Moscow landlady's house, who saves a puppy he names Mumu, raises it, and is then ordered by the landlady to drown it because the dog disturbs her nerves. The story was written during Turgenev's house arrest at Spasskoye following the Government's objection to his Gogol obituary and is based on an actual event in the household of his mother, one of the cruelest serf-owners in the region.",
