    intro: "The Seagull (1896) is Anton Chekhov's first major theatrical success — after its notorious disastrous premiere in St Petersburg in 1896, it was revived by the Moscow Art Theatre in 1898 and became the play that established Chekhov's dramatic reputation. The story of a group of people on a lake estate — the faded actress Irina Arkadina, her son Konstantin who wants to write a new kind of theatre, the famous writer Trigorin whom Arkadina loves, the young Nina who falls in love with Trigorin and becomes his mistress — is a meditation on art, love, fame, and the cost of both having and not having talent.",
