    intro: "Uncle Vanya (1898) is Anton Chekhov's most perfectly constructed play — the story of the inhabitants of a provincial Russian estate: Vanya (who has managed the estate for his brother-in-law Serebryakov for twenty years, sacrificing his own life for what he thought was a great man), Sonya (who loves Dr Astrov, who doesn't love her back), and Dr Astrov himself (who loves the forest, and Yelena, who does not love him). When Serebryakov arrives and proposes to sell the estate, the fragile equilibrium of the household shatters. It is the most concentrated of the four major Chekhov plays and, for many readers, the most devastating.",
