    intro: "Childhood (1852) is Leo Tolstoy's first published work — the autobiographical account of the childhood years of Nikolenka Irtenyev, a Russian nobleman. It was immediately recognized as an extraordinary debut, establishing Tolstoy's characteristic technique of what he called 'the dialectic of the soul' — the attempt to trace the actual movement of thought and feeling rather than only its results. Childhood was followed by Boyhood (1854) and Youth (1857) to form a trilogy.",
