    intro: "White Nights (1848) is Fyodor Dostoevsky's most lyrical short work — the tale of an unnamed dreamer who, during the white nights of the St Petersburg summer, meets a young woman named Nastenka weeping on an embankment, listens to her story, falls in love with her, and loses her when the man she has been waiting for finally returns. The novella is the most concentrated expression of the Dostoevskian 'dreamer' type — the man who lives in his imagination rather than in reality.",
