    slug: 'notes-dead-house-dostoevsky',
    intro: "Notes from a Dead House (1862) is Fyodor Dostoevsky's fictionalized memoir of his four years in a Siberian prison camp — one of the first major works of prison literature in any language. The narrator Aleksandr Petrovich Goryanchikov, a nobleman convicted of murdering his wife, describes the world of the prison camp in Omsk: the characters of his fellow prisoners, the daily routine, the punishments, the occasional moments of relief. The book transformed Dostoevsky's understanding of the Russian people and is foundational to his subsequent work.",
