    intro: "The Eternal Husband (1870) is Fyodor Dostoevsky's most brilliant short novel — a psychological duel between Velchaninov, a middle-aged bachelor who has had many affairs, and Pavel Pavlovich Trusotsky, the 'eternal husband' of Dostoevsky's title — the man who always ends up cuckolded, who knows it, and who in this case has tracked Velchaninov down after his wife's death. The novel is the most tightly constructed of Dostoevsky's shorter works and one of the supreme achievements of Russian psychological fiction.",
