    intro: "A Diary of a Writer (1873–1881) is Fyodor Dostoevsky's most unusual work — a monthly journal that he wrote, edited, and published himself for most of the last decade of his life. The Diary contains essays, short stories (including the celebrated 'The Meek One' and 'The Dream of a Ridiculous Man'), political commentary, literary criticism, and personal reminiscences. It is the most direct expression of Dostoevsky's complex political and religious views.",
    startWith: "The Meek One (from A Diary of a Writer)",
