    intro: "Winter Notes on Summer Impressions (1863) is Fyodor Dostoevsky's account of his first journey to Western Europe in 1862 — to Germany, France, England, and Switzerland. It is one of the founding texts of Russian anti-Western critique: Dostoevsky presents the European cities (particularly London and Paris) as evidence of what bourgeois civilization actually produces when its premises are followed to their conclusion, and contrasts this with his vision of the Russian people's different spiritual resources.",
