    slug: 'mtsyri-lermontov',
    intro: "Mtsyri (1840) is Lermontov's second major narrative poem — the story of a young Caucasian captive who has grown up in a Georgian monastery and escapes for three days into the mountains before being found dying near the walls. In those three days he encounters nature, a Georgian girl, a battle with a leopard, and the homeland he had dreamed of — and discovers he cannot survive freedom.",
    startWith: "Mtsyri",
