    startWith: "Bar Mitzvah Boy (1976) by Jack Rosenthal — the companion in his career — the BBC Play for Today examining what the relationship between a thirteen-year-old Jewish boy, his approaching bar mitzvah, and the family and social world that are all expecting him to go through with it looks like from inside the boy inside that relationship — the companion in his sustained examination of what the relationship between ordinary people and specific social and institutional processes looks like from inside the ordinary people inside it.",
