    slug: 'mike-leigh-four-days-in-july',
    intro: "Four Days in July (1985) by Mike Leigh is a television film set in Belfast, Northern Ireland, about two couples — one Catholic, one Protestant — who are both expecting babies around the same time and who are both navigating the ordinary anxieties of new parenthood inside the extraordinary context of the Troubles. The film examines what ordinary life looks like from inside the ordinary people inside it when the context of that ordinary life is one of ongoing political violence and sectarian division — what the relationship between the ordinary human experiences of love, birth, and family and the political and sectarian context that surrounds them looks like from inside the people inside all of it. These books share its interest in what ordinary life looks like when it is being lived inside an extraordinary context.",
