    slug: 'michael-apted-7-up',
    intro: "7 Up (1964) and the subsequent Up series by Michael Apted is a documentary series that returns every seven years to the same group of people, first filmed as seven-year-olds in 1964, to examine what their lives have become and what the relationship between the children they were and the people they have become looks like across the decades. The series examines what the relationship between a person's origins — their class, their family, their circumstance — and their life looks like when that relationship is examined repeatedly from the outside over a period of more than fifty years. These books share its interest in what the relationship between who a person was and who they have become looks like when that relationship is examined over time.",
    startWith: "The Up Series (2012) by Michael Apted — the companion in its own ongoing form — the continuation of the series through 56 Up (2012) and 63 Up (2019) and beyond, in which the same people continue to be revisited and what the relationship between their lives and the passage of time continues to be examined from inside the people inside it.",
