    intro: "Artist Descending a Staircase (1972) by Tom Stoppard is a radio play — originally written for BBC Radio 3 — about three artists who have been friends since before the First World War and what has happened to them across their lives. It uses a complex non-linear structure, moving backwards and forwards through the decades, as the two surviving artists try to work out what killed the third. It is one of Stoppard's most formally elegant works — the palindromic structure, in which the play proceeds forwards and then retraces its steps, is perfectly realised — and it is also one of his most affecting, about friendship and art and memory and what is lost across a long life. These books share its interest in friendship across time and the formal possibilities of non-linear narrative.",
