    slug: 'edward-bond-summer',
    intro: "Summer (1982) by Edward Bond is a play set on an Adriatic island in which a German woman, Marthe, returns with her daughter to the island where she spent the war years. A local woman, Xenia, whose family owned the house that the German officer stayed in during the occupation, meets them and what is revealed in the encounter is the specific history of the occupation and what Xenia knows about what happened. The play is quiet and conversational but it accumulates to a revelation about complicity and what people do and do not know about what was done in their proximity. These books share its interest in what war leaves behind and what people know and don't say and what the encounter between those who were there from different positions reveals.",
