    intro: "Chiaroscuro (1986) by Jackie Kay is a play about four Black British women — Beth, a Black woman adopted by a white family; Aisha, a Black woman of mixed heritage; and two others — and what they talk about together: identity, sexuality, race, belonging. The play was written for the Theatre of Black Women and examines what it means to be Black and a woman in Britain in the 1980s, what it means to have multiple possible identities, and what sisterhood means when the women in a room have very different relationships to their Blackness. These books share its interest in what Black British women's experience looks like and what the question of identity means when you are living at the intersection of multiple categories.",
