    intro: "Beneatha's Place (2013) by Kwame Kwei-Armah is a response to Lorraine Hansberry's A Raisin in the Sun, set in a restaurant in Baltimore some fifty years after the events of Hansberry's play. Beneatha Younger — who in Hansberry's play dreamed of becoming a doctor and of Africa — is now an old woman, and the play examines what has happened to her dream and to the world she was part of. These books share its interest in what the Black experience in America and Britain looks like across generations and what happens when you revisit the founding texts of Black political aspiration.",
