    intro: "Play Mas (1974) by Mustapha Matura is a play set in Trinidad on the eve of Independence in 1962. Samuel, a tailor, is approached by politicians who want to use him and his shop as part of the Independence Day celebrations — they want him to make the costumes for the carnival. The play is about what independence actually means for ordinary people in Trinidad and what the political class does with the idea of independence versus what it means on the street. These books share its interest in what political independence looks like from the inside and what happens when the celebration of liberation is organised by those who are going to benefit from power.",
