    slug: 'david-greig-dunsinane',
    intro: "Dunsinane (2010) by David Greig is a sequel to Shakespeare's Macbeth. The English army has defeated Macbeth and installed Malcolm as king of Scotland. A young English officer, Siward, is left in command of the English forces occupying Scotland. The play follows what happens as Siward tries to hold the occupation together — as the Scots refuse to cooperate, as Gruach (the woman known as Lady Macbeth) refuses to accept her defeat, and as Siward discovers that the situation is far more complicated than any narrative of good versus evil allows. These books share its interest in what occupations look like from the inside and what Shakespeare's Macbeth means when seen from the Scottish side.",
