    intro: "How to Hold Your Breath (2015) by Zinnie Harris is a play about the austerity crisis in Europe and what it does to ordinary people. Dana is a young British woman who meets and sleeps with a stranger, Jarron, who reveals himself to be the devil. As Dana travels through Europe — through countries in the grip of financial collapse, austerity, and the human consequences of economic crises — Jarron is always there, and the world becomes increasingly dark. The play is a fable about what neoliberal economics does to people and what the devil looks like when he wears the face of a financial crisis. These books share its interest in the European austerity crisis and what it did to the people inside it.",
