    intro: "Our Country's Good (1988) by Timberlake Wertenbaker is based on Thomas Keneally's novel The Playmaker. It is set in the first British convict colony in Australia in 1788-89, where a young officer, Second Lieutenant Ralph Clark, is organising a production of George Farquhar's The Recruiting Officer with a cast of convicts. The play examines what theatre does — what it is for, what the act of making a play does to the people involved — through the story of this actual production among the first generation of convict settlers. It is one of the most celebrated British plays of the 1980s. These books share its interest in what the first Australian colony was and what theatre does for people in extreme circumstances.",
