    intro: "Five Finger Exercise (1958) by Peter Shaffer is a domestic drama about a German tutor, Walter, who comes to live with an upper-middle-class English family in Suffolk. Each member of the family wants something different from Walter: the mother Pamela wants a cultured companion; the father Stanley wants to be confirmed in his anti-intellectual prejudices; the daughter Clive wants a friend; the son Charles develops a different kind of attachment. Walter, a refugee from post-war Germany with his own hidden anguish, cannot be all these things at once. The play is a precise examination of what the English class system does to everyone inside it, from the educated working-class father who has made money to the Oxbridge-educated son who despises the house he grew up in. These books share its interest in what class and education do in 1950s England and what Shaffer was doing at the start of his career.",
