    intro: "Death and the King's Horseman (1975) by Wole Soyinka is based on historical events in Nigeria in 1946: Elesin, the horseman of the Alafin of Oyo, is required by Yoruba custom to follow his king into death. The British colonial officer Simon Pilkings intervenes to stop the ritual suicide, believing he is preventing a waste of life. His intervention fails — but the failure, and who dies as a result, is the subject of the play. Soyinka calls it a 'clash of civilisations' but insists it is not primarily about colonialism — it is about Elesin's failure of will, his choice to delay the ritual for a personal pleasure. These books share its interest in what Yoruba culture is, what ritual means, and what colonialism does when it intervenes in what it does not understand.",
