    intro: "The Philanthropist (1970) by Christopher Hampton is a comedy about Philip, a university lecturer in linguistics who agrees with everything everyone says and is consequently unable to form any real relationship, set in a world in which a playwright has just shot himself because his play received bad reviews. The play is a response to Molière's Le Misanthrope — in which the central character hates everyone — and it asks what happens when you replace misanthropy with its opposite: a man who loves everyone and so loves no one. These books share its interest in what academic life is, what linguistic analysis does to its practitioners, and what comedy looks like when it examines what it means to have no opinions of your own.",
