    intro: "Dana H. (2019) by Lucas Hnath is one of the most formally radical American plays of the last decade — the entire play is the playwright's mother Dana speaking, recorded from hours of interviews, and the actress playing her (Deirdre O'Connell in the original production) lip-syncs to the recordings with extreme precision; the story Dana tells is of being held captive for five months by a man she met while doing pastoral work, and what that experience did to her faith, her life, and her relationship to language.",
