    slug: 'little-women-alcott',
    intro: "Little Women (1868) is Louisa May Alcott's most beloved novel — the story of the four March sisters, Meg, Jo, Beth, and Amy, growing up in New England during the Civil War while their father is away. Jo March is one of the great characters in American fiction: passionate, ambitious, tomboyish, a writer who burns her manuscript when her sister reads it without permission and who refuses the marriage proposal of her neighbor Laurie because she knows herself well enough to know it would be wrong. The novel has been in print continuously since publication and has shaped the reading lives of women and girls for over a century.",
    startWith: "Little Women",
