    slug: 'cold-comfort-farm-gibbons',
    intro: "Cold Comfort Farm (1932) is Stella Gibbons's debut novel and one of the great English comic novels — a parody of the rural Gothic tradition (Mary Webb, D.H. Lawrence's pastoral mode) in which Flora Poste, a sensible modern young woman newly orphaned, goes to live with her distant relatives the Starkadders at Cold Comfort Farm in Sussex. The Starkadders are a collection of Gothic rural types — the deranged matriarch Aunt Ada Doom who saw 'something nasty in the woodshed,' the brooding Seth, the religious zealot Amos — and Flora proceeds to sort them all out with cheerful efficiency. The novel is very funny and very well-written, and it has accumulated a cult readership that extends well beyond the rural-Gothic readers it was initially parodying.",
