    intro: "The Marriage Plot (2011) is Jeffrey Eugenides's third novel — a love triangle set at Brown University in the early 1980s, following Madeleine Hanna, who is writing her senior thesis on the marriage plot in Victorian fiction, and her two competing suitors: Leonard Bankhead, a brilliant and emotionally volatile biology student who turns out to have bipolar disorder, and Mitchell Grammaticus, a religious studies major who goes to India to work with Mother Teresa and comes back changed. The novel is about literary theory and its limits, about the difference between the love you read about and the love you actually live, and about what happens when someone you love is genuinely ill.",
