    slug: 'good-omens-gaiman',
    intro: "Good Omens (1990) is the collaborative novel by Neil Gaiman and Terry Pratchett — a comedy about the coming of the Antichrist and the apocalypse, told from the perspective of an angel named Aziraphale and a demon named Crowley who have been stationed on Earth since the Garden of Eden and who have grown rather fond of it. When the Antichrist is accidentally given to the wrong family and grows up as a perfectly normal boy in an English village, the ineffable plan begins to go wrong, and Aziraphale and Crowley find themselves working together — against Heaven and Hell both — to prevent the end of the world. The novel is very funny, very warm, and one of the essential comic-fantasy novels in English.",
