    slug: 'bridge-sighs-russo',
    intro: "Bridge of Sighs (2007) is Richard Russo's most ambitious novel — a long, introspective book about two men from the same small upstate New York town, Thomaston, whose lives have diverged completely. Lou Lynch, who stayed in Thomaston and built a life there as a small businessman and father, is writing the memoir of his life; Bobby Noonan, who left for Venice and became an artist, is refusing to come home for the reunion that Lou is planning. Russo weaves between Lou's memoir, the present, and the past to construct a portrait of the forces that make people who they are and of what it costs to stay in a place and what it costs to leave.",
