    slug: 'mohawk-russo',
    intro: "Mohawk (1986) is Richard Russo's debut novel, set in the same fictional upstate New York mill town that appears in The Risk Pool (1988). It introduces the world Russo would develop for the next three decades: a declining industrial town, a cast of working-class characters whose lives intersect at the local diner and bar, and the combination of comedy and elegy that would become his signature. Though less accomplished than his later novels, Mohawk establishes the milieu, the voice, and several of the concerns — economic decline, masculine failure, small-town community — that Russo pursued throughout his career.",
