    intro: "That Old Cape Magic (2009) is Richard Russo's most autobiographical novel — a quiet, personal book about Jack Griffin, a screenwriter and former English professor, whose parents' troubled marriage centered on annual vacations to Cape Cod, a place they loved and that Jack associates with both his parents' best selves and their fundamental incompatibility. The novel follows Jack across two family weddings — his daughter's, and his wife's — as he tries to scatter the ashes of each parent and as the truth of his own marriage comes gradually into focus. It is shorter and more meditative than most of Russo's work, closer to memoir in spirit.",
