    intro: "Chances Are... (2019) is Richard Russo's most recent novel — a thriller-adjacent story of three men who were college roommates in the late 1960s, who reunite on Martha's Vineyard forty years later, and who are still haunted by the disappearance of Jacy Calloway, a fourth friend who vanished over that same Memorial Day weekend in 1971. Russo writes the reunion weekend with his characteristic warmth and comedy, but the mystery of what happened to Jacy generates a genuine suspense that runs beneath the social surface. It is a departure in some ways — shorter, more plot-driven, more consciously thriller-structured — but unmistakably his.",
