    slug: 'tree-of-smoke-johnson',
    intro: "Tree of Smoke (2007) is Denis Johnson's National Book Award-winning Vietnam War novel — his longest and most ambitious book, following a cast of characters whose lives are shaped and destroyed by the war over the decade from 1963 to 1983. At its center is Skip Sands, a CIA operative working for his uncle, the legendary Colonel Francis Sands, on a classified psychological operations project called 'Tree of Smoke'; alongside him are two American brothers from Phoenix who enlist, a Canadian missionary nurse, and a Vietnamese double agent. Johnson does not write the conventional war novel — there are no battles in the traditional sense — but instead a novel about what the war does to the people who pass through it and the lies that sustain it.",
