    slug: 'fiskadoro-johnson',
    intro: "Fiskadoro (1985) is Denis Johnson's most formally experimental novel — a post-apocalyptic work set in the Florida Keys decades after a nuclear war, following a boy named Fiskadoro who wants to learn the clarinet from a jazz musician named Mr. Cheung, whose family has survived across several generations in the ruins of a civilization. The novel alternates between Fiskadoro's present-day story and the memories of Mr. Cheung's grandmother, who as a young Vietnamese girl survived the fall of Saigon and the refugee camps. Johnson uses the post-apocalyptic setting to explore what survives catastrophe — not technology or ideology but music, ritual, and the body's capacity for ceremony — and the result is one of the most underrated American novels of the 1980s.",
