    intro: "The Orchard Keeper (1965) is Cormac McCarthy's debut novel, set in the mountains of eastern Tennessee during the 1930s and 1940s. It follows three intersecting lives — a young man, an aging moonshiner, and a reclusive orchard keeper — in a remote community where the old ways of the hills are giving way to a modernizing world. McCarthy's prose, already dense and biblical, draws on Faulkner and the Southern Gothic tradition, and the novel established many of the concerns he would pursue throughout his career: violence, isolation, the relationship between men and the natural world, and the passing of an older America.",
    startWith: "The Orchard Keeper",
