    slug: 'all-pretty-horses-mccarthy',
    intro: "All the Pretty Horses (1992) is the first volume of Cormac McCarthy's Border Trilogy and the novel that brought him from critical cult figure to wide readership, winning the National Book Award. Set in 1949–1950, it follows sixteen-year-old John Grady Cole, whose family ranch in Texas is being sold, as he rides south into Mexico with his friend Lacey Rawlins in search of a world that still has a place for young men who can work horses. What they find is both the paradise John Grady sought and its destruction: a great hacienda where he proves himself a brilliant horsebreaker, a dangerous love affair with the hacendado's daughter, and an imprisonment in a Mexican jail that tests everything in him.",
