    intro: "The Secret Agent (1907) by Joseph Conrad is the darkest comedy in the English novel and one of Conrad's most formally perfect books — the story of Mr. Verloc, a lazy double agent who runs a pornography shop in London as his cover while feeding information to an unnamed European power's embassy. When the embassy grows impatient and demands a provocation — the bombing of the Greenwich Observatory — Verloc's attempt to delegate the task to his wife's simple-minded younger brother Stevie triggers a catastrophe that destroys everyone around him. Conrad set the novel in 1886 London and based it partly on a real anarchist bombing attempt near Greenwich in 1894; he described it as 'a simple tale of the XIX century' and 'a tale of darkness.' Its London is a city of fog, sewers, and moral nullity — the anarchists and police equally corrupt, equally hollow, equally devoted to their own self-preservation.",
