    slug: 'the-ambassadors-james',
    intro: "The Ambassadors (1903) by Henry James is the novel James himself considered his most technically perfect — the story of Lambert Strether, a middle-aged editor from Woollett, Massachusetts, sent to Paris by his prospective fiancée Mrs. Newsome to retrieve her son Chad from what she assumes is a corrupting entanglement with a French woman. What Strether finds instead is that Chad has been refined and improved by Europe, and that the Parisian world of Madame de Vionnet and the milieu she represents offers a vision of civilized life that Woollett has never imagined. The novel is James's most sustained meditation on the theme of living — 'Live all you can; it's a mistake not to' — and the tragedy of those who arrive at this understanding too late.",
