    intro: "Joseph Conrad's Victory (1915) is his most romantic and his most metaphysical novel — the story of Axel Heyst, a philosophical recluse who has retreated from the world to a remote island in the Malay Archipelago, and the woman he rescues from a hotel orchestra in Surabaya. When three men arrive on the island, Heyst's philosophy of detachment — his conviction that the best strategy in life is to 'not leave a trace' — is tested against the violent world he had hoped to escape. Victory is Conrad's most direct engagement with the question of whether a life lived in non-attachment can survive an encounter with the full violence of human desire.",
