    intro: "Charles Dickens's Dombey and Son (1846–48) is one of his most psychologically ambitious novels — the story of Mr. Paul Dombey, the cold, proud merchant who cares only for his son and heir, and who destroys through his emotional incapacity almost everything he loves. Often called the first Dickens novel to be fully planned in advance, it marks the transition between the relatively picaresque early novels and the mature social panoramas of Bleak House and Our Mutual Friend.",
    startWith: 'Dombey and Son',
