    intro: "Thomas Hardy's The Mayor of Casterbridge (1886) is one of his most Shakespearean novels — a study in self-destruction organized around Michael Henchard, a hay-trusser who sells his wife and daughter while drunk at a fair and spends the rest of his life trying to recover from the consequences, becoming mayor of the Dorset town of Casterbridge only to be progressively destroyed by the return of his past. Hardy called it 'a story of a man of character.'",
