    intro: "William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet (c. 1594–1596) is the most famous love story in the English language — a five-day tragedy about two young people from feuding families in Verona who fall in love and die as a result, whose names have become universal shorthand for doomed romance. The play has been performed continuously for four centuries, adapted into opera, ballet, film, and musical, and is typically the first Shakespeare play most readers encounter.",
