    intro: "Dante Alighieri's Divine Comedy (c. 1308–1321) is the supreme work of Italian literature and one of the greatest long poems in any language — an epic in three parts (Inferno, Purgatorio, Paradiso) following Dante through the afterlife guided by the Roman poet Virgil and then by his idealized love Beatrice, providing a comprehensive medieval vision of sin, redemption, and the divine order. The Inferno, with its vivid circles of Hell, is the most widely read and culturally influential section.",
