    slug: 'glass-castle',
    intro: "Jeannette Walls's The Glass Castle (2005) is a memoir of growing up with Rex and Rose Mary Walls, parents who were brilliant, alcoholic, and profoundly neglectful — who moved their four children across the American Southwest and Appalachia in a series of ramshackle houses, living on the fringe of society, with Rex always promising to build his children a glass castle someday. One of the bestselling memoirs of the twenty-first century, The Glass Castle is about poverty, parental failure, love that coexists with damage, and the story we tell ourselves about the family we had.",
    startWith: 'The Glass Castle',
